  "googleDriveHelpSameAccountTitle": "Same Google account on another device",
  "googleDriveHelpSameAccountBody": "1. On this device: set a sync passphrase, then Sign in with Google.\n2. On the other device: Sign in with the same Google account and enter the exact same passphrase.\n3. Sync runs automatically after login and when you tap Sync now. Nothing else to configure.",
  "googleDriveHelpCrossAccountTitle": "Different Google accounts",
  "googleDriveHelpCrossAccountBody": "Account 1 (owner):\n1. Set a sync passphrase and Sign in with Google.\n2. Under “Share with another account”, enter account 2’s email and share.\n\nAccount 2 (joiner):\n1. Tap “Join a sync someone shared with you”.\n2. Sign in with Google (broader Drive permission is requested so the app can find the shared file).\n3. Pick the shared sync file, then enter the exact same passphrase account 1 used.\n4. Sync now pulls and merges data both ways through that shared file.",
  "googleDriveHelpPassphraseNote": "The passphrase never leaves the device — Google only stores encrypted data. Everyone who syncs together must know and enter the same passphrase.",
  "googleDriveHelpRegenNote": "If you regenerate or change the passphrase after connecting, other devices and accounts stop decrypting until they enter the new passphrase too.",
